<title>USA: InterVoice to sell systems in Mexico.</title>
<headline>InterVoice to sell systems in Mexico.</headline>
<dateline>DALLAS 1996-11-05</dateline>
<text>
<p>InterVoice Inc said on Tuesday Mexico's electric utility company has agreed to purchase 61 InterVoice call and business process automation systems representing more than 1,200 ports.</p>
<p>The sale for an undisclosed amount was made by Siemens AG, a global distributor of InterVoice solutions, in conjunction with Kranon,  an InterVoice reseller based in Mexico City, the company said.</p>
<p>Shipment of the InterVoice systems will take place during the company's current fiscal quarter.</p>
</text>
